# Java Formatting

## Rules

- 4-space indent, no tabs (`.editorconfig`)
- UTF-8, LF line endings, trim trailing whitespace
- Google Java Format **AOSP style** via Spotless (not Spring Java Format)

## Commands

```bash
./mvnw spotless:apply          # fix formatting
./mvnw spotless:check          # verify (also runs on verify phase)
./scripts/check.sh spotless    # quiet check with one-line output
```

## Do

- Run Spotless after editing Java files; `./scripts/check.sh spotless` is part of the verification workflow
- If Spotless fails: run `spotless:apply`, then `spotless:check` (or `check.sh spotless`) — do not hand-fix style
- Match existing import style; Spotless removes unused imports
- Use `final` utility classes with private constructors for helpers

## Don't

- Use tabs in Java, XML, or YAML
- Add Spring Java Format config (`.springjavaformatconfig`) — not used in this project
- Hand-format against Spotless output
